 ## Background
-Chunk mesh generation originated in Minecraft, which groups blocks into $16 \times 16 \times 16$ chunks and renders only visible faces as a single mesh per chunk [S2, unofficial]. This approach was adopted in various voxel engines and mods (e.g., Sodium, Greedy Meshing mod) to optimize rendering performance [S4, S5, unofficial]. It is a precursor to more advanced greedy meshing techniques that merge adjacent faces into larger quads [Greedy Meshing / Face Culling](8774-greedy-meshing-face-culling.md).
